/tmp/tmp.y7X5pe7ToP/further_work.tex:3:This work presents a general McEliece-like encryption frame for matrix codes whose security is based on the MinRank problem. We propose a general masking for rank codes that we apply on a matrix code version of Gabidulin vector code. We define a new problem: the Enhanced Gabidulin Matrix Code (EGMC) distinguishing problem, for which we propose a thorough analysis and study possible distinguishers to solve it. It results in a competitive encryption scheme, which achieves a ciphertext size of 65B for 128 bits of security.
/tmp/tmp.y7X5pe7ToP/further_work.tex:7:%This work presents a general frame to construct encryption schemes based on the MinRank problem. We proposed an adaptation of the McEliece and Niederreiter frames to matrix codes, by masking a code for which we know an efficient decoding algorithm with a transformation having a trapdoor. Such codes are easy to obtain, by considering matrix versions of vector codes. We propose an encryption scheme by applying these ideas to a Gabidulin code. It resulsts a competitive encryption scheme, which achieves a ciphertext size of 65 B for 128 bits of security.
