/tmp/tmp.y7X5pe7ToP/new_schemes.tex:170:The most costly step for the key generation is the multiplication by the matrices $\Pv$ and $\Qv$. It involves computing $km$ products of the form $\Pv \Av_i \Qv$, which requires $km ((m + \ell_1)^2 (m + \ell_2) + (m + \ell_2)^2 (m + \ell_1))$ multiplications in $\Fq$. For the Neiderreiter variant, we must also consider the cost of computing the matrix $\bar{\Hv}$, which can be done using Gaussian elimination, giving a complexity of $\mathcal{O}(((m + \ell_1)(m + \ell_2))^3)$ operations in $\Fq$.
