/tmp/tmp.y7X5pe7ToP/diff.tex:668:The Niederreiter frame is a variant of the McEliece frame for code-based encryption, which consists in hiding a parity check matrix rather than a generator matrix. It allows to obtain syndromes as ciphertexts, which are shorter than noisy code words for an equivalent security, since the MinRank problem and the MinRank-Syndrome problem are equivalent. \DIFdelbegin \DIFdel{However, it is not possible in the case of matrix codes to retrieve the original message by directly hiding a base of the dual code. Consequently, we give in the public key the control matrix of a previously hidden code. }\DIFdelend The resulting scheme can be found in Figure \ref{mr-nie}.
