The audit uncovered two substantive issues in the partial module. First, its native construction and Section 7 parameter row are faithful, but its G8 key only handles permutations—not the full basis/isometry symmetries of a matrix code. Second, and more serious, it counts only 161 output symbols as the “compact route”; finding those random symbols still requires a large MinRank computation. I’m measuring the implementation now and will either repair the family around a genuine sub-300-operation insight or document a gate-level rejection rather than certify that shortcut fiction.
